WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.185
Continuous monitoring helps organizations maintain awareness of changing security posture, system state, threats, vulnerabilities, control effectiveness, and risk.

2
00:00:11.185 --> 00:00:20.149
It is the practice of watching the things that matter after launch, after authorization, after deployment, and after the last assessment.

3
00:00:20.149 --> 00:00:23.980
Systems change, threats change, and business use changes.

4
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:29.036
Monitoring helps teams see those changes while there is still time to respond.

5
00:00:29.036 --> 00:00:36.391
Effective monitoring is scoped, risk-based, evidence-driven, owned, reviewed, and connected to remediation.

6
00:00:36.391 --> 00:00:47.346
It should cover assets, identities, configurations, vulnerabilities, logs, changes, alerts, incidents, and controls in a way that matches risk and business context.

7
00:00:47.346 --> 00:00:57.689
The program should prioritize critical systems, sensitive data, privileged access, exposed services, known weaknesses, and mission-important workflows.

8
00:00:57.689 --> 00:01:02.745
Strong monitoring depends on telemetry quality and operational discipline.

9
00:01:02.745 --> 00:01:04.201
Logs must be reliable.

10
00:01:04.201 --> 00:01:06.806
Evidence must be current and traceable.

11
00:01:06.806 --> 00:01:08.338
Alerts must be triaged.

12
00:01:08.338 --> 00:01:10.100
Findings must have owners.

13
00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.169
Exceptions must be documented.

14
00:01:12.169 --> 00:01:14.314
Reports must support decisions.

15
00:01:14.314 --> 00:01:17.455
Control evidence must reflect real operations.

16
00:01:17.455 --> 00:01:25.269
Without those habits, monitoring can become a noisy data collection exercise rather than a risk management capability.

17
00:01:25.269 --> 00:01:27.644
The goal is not collecting more data.

18
00:01:27.644 --> 00:01:33.084
The goal is making better security and risk decisions faster and more consistently.

19
00:01:33.084 --> 00:01:42.890
Continuous monitoring should help teams understand what changed, what matters, who owns it, what action is needed, and how the program should improve.

20
00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:48.943
That is what turns monitoring from passive observation into practical security operations.
